Z||000007||tgowens||06-13-2001||10:40 AM||||Larry, as I mentioned in an earlier thread, I have been contacted about designing a national web site for F.O.C.O.A. - I am currently awaiting the decision of the Regional Directors before completing this project and that decision should be made soon. As I understand it, it is now in the hands of the 77 member clubs for their approval. <P>Let me mention once again, that FOCOA is a business AND a club - the <I>business</I> is managed by Phil and Gloria while the <I>club</I> is managed by the Board of Directors consisting of the Regional Directors of the eight national regions.<P>Just so that you know, the present web site evidently has been deleted. I do know that there are changes being made even at this moment and there <I>will</I> be a new FOCOA web site soon!!<P>Oh, by the way, the web site you see when using the link of fieroowners.com is <B>not</B> <I>my</I> design -- i'm not really sure <I>whose</I> design that one is!!||||reg||1
Z||000008||kslish||06-13-2001||04:27 PM||||First off, I want to say that this message is not to offend anyone working with F.O.C.O.A. directly.  I have been a supporter of F.O.C.O.A. (but not always their business practices) and have enjoyed the National Conventions the years that I have been able to attend, but they just keep dropping the ball again and again.  We are 7 weeks away from the Williamsburg show and not only does their website no longer function (that porno site forwarding is great P.R. work, I guess someone let the domain name registration expire) but the e-mail addresses that are on the Williamburg registration form no longer work to e-mail F.O.C.O.A.  <P>To those that are aware of what is going on, and know about the upcoming new web site, this may not be a big deal.  But looking at it from another point of view, it's not very encouraging to a Fiero owner looking for information or to register for the Williamsburg show that may not be on this message board or other Fiero e-mail distribution lists.<P>Basically I'm saying changes should be made in the off-season (winter), not right before a major event.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by tgowens:<BR><B>As I understand it, it is now in the hands of the 77 member clubs for their approval.</B><BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Who exactly is the regional director for the northeast and/or Pennsylvania?  I'd like to share my concerns with them.  The West Penn Fiero Club is suppossed to be one of those 77 member clubs but this is the first I've heard of a lot of this and nothing has been presented to us to approve.<P>I will say tgowens it's about time they got someone like you to design a decent professional site for them...can't wait to see it.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>West Penn Fiero Club webmaster and secretary<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A><p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 06-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||tgowens||06-13-2001||06:26 PM||||Ken, the Regional Director for the New England Region is showing to be Fran Passuite. Unfortunately there is no contact listing for Fran on the list that I have so I would suggest that you contact Joe Goodmon at 4nyjoe@home.com as he is the National Secretary as I understand it - voice your concerns with him as I have no further information other than what I have presented to you.<P>Also, inform him of what you get when you look for the national web site -- maybe that will spur things on...........<P>I hope this helps...........<P>Terry<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>                  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero/3GTS_SIG.gif">                   </A>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Old Lar||06-13-2001||07:10 PM||||Fran lives in Lockport, NY, about 1 hour from me.  The last I knew he had no home computer, but was looking into it.  His grandchildren would teach him how to use it.<P>I didnot know there were 77 member clubs in FOCOA.  With that many organizations supporting the Fiero cause, the national club should be hopping.<P>Get that web site up and going.  Easier said than done, I know Terry.||||reg||1
